# Panel updates — commit + push on `dev`

Operator standing preference: **always commit + push after panel updates**.

## When this applies

After a ready change that ships via **Settings → Updates** — especially under `web-nodejs/` (`public/js`, views, locales, services tied to the panel updater) — **commit on `dev` and `git push origin dev` in the same session**. Do not leave panel-only fixes uncommitted/unpushed waiting for a separate ask.

Same habit for **agent standing-workflow rules** under `.cursor/rules/` when Ole wants them persisted (see `chesster1981-fork-workflow.mdc`).

## Rules

1. Target branch: **`dev`** (day-to-day), not `main`.
2. Push: `git push origin dev` on **Chesster1981/BetterDesk** — never UNITRONIX unless Ole explicitly asks; never force-push unless the operator explicitly requests it.
3. Confirm `git remote -v` shows Chesster1981 before pushing.
4. If the same logical fix also touches `rdclient-desktop` Rust, include those files in the **same** commit, then push.
5. Do **not** stage secrets (`.env`, credentials), `rdclient-desktop/dist-release/` binaries, or unrelated junk.
6. Override: if the operator says **"don't push"** (or equivalent) for that task, skip the push.
7. Do **not** open UNITRONIX PRs as part of this habit.

## Checklist

- [ ] On `dev` (or feature branch off `dev` as directed)
- [ ] Only relevant fix files staged
- [ ] Commit created
- [ ] Pushed to Chesster1981 `origin/dev` (unless overridden)
